{
  "note": [
    "Layer-3 labels: what a slot MEANS on one engine, for printing on a control surface.",
    "The address a control binds to is always the generic layer-2 one ('/sk/a/param/speed');",
    "this file only decides what is printed on it ('station'). Cosmetic by construction - a",
    "label that rots misnames a fader and can never make the device unreachable.",
    "",
    "This is a stand-in for the `param_label()` hook docs/dev/terminal-osc.md proposes on IEngine.",
    "When that lands, `describe` carries the labels and scripts/gen_tosc.py --describe reads them",
    "from the device instead, at which point this file is a fallback for offline generation.",
    "",
    "Keys are '<kind>:<slot>' with kind = param | cfg and slot the layer-2 wire name from",
    "src/terminal/names.cpp. Sourced from the Controls table in docs/engines/<engine>.md.",
    "An engine with no entry, or a slot with no entry, prints its layer-2 name - degraded,",
    "never broken (document, translation rule 4). ASCII, lowercase, short enough for a caption."
  ],
  "engines": {
    "radio": {
      "param:speed": "station",
      "param:pos": "start",
      "param:size": "varispeed",
      "param:env": "static",
      "param:mix": "volume",
      "param:aux": "bank",
      "param:crossfade": "blend",
      "cfg:route": "stereo image"
    },
